{
	title: 'Tool card titles lead with the lowercase tool name',
	spec: 'A tool card title starts with its tool name in lowercase, followed by its object (toolDetails.headline returns the name as mark): bash <description> for BASH, with the command on the next row unprefixed and & beside the card id when backgrounded; read <paths, cut off with …> for READ, read_blob and read_entry likewise; edit <files> for EDIT, + before a created file, - before a deleted one, and per-file line counts (foo.ts +2-2) only when the whole row fits; send <target> for SEND, the message below; wait for <targets> for WAIT; notify <text>; spawn <id> (tab N): <name>, then (interactive) or (autoclose ↧), nothing for a subagent left open; stop <target>; help <tool>; inspect <target>; google <query>; other tools likewise. A slash command reads as typed: it starts with /. Incoming messages from other sessions and tasks read <= <sender> (tab N, delivery), with delivery steering, next round or queued; soft-steering is not shown in titles. A finished background command reads <= Background command finished (exit N) with the ↑ t<call> link of a detached output card. A Hal reply ending in a question is headed ? Hal (<model>). Prompts and commands the user typed are unchanged. The web has no room for names: where a tool has an icon it shows the icon and drops the name, and bash shows its copyable $ instead.',
